{
  "about": "Test vectors for the launch fingerprint the Linux supervisor (apps/bridge/src/supervisor/launch-approval.ts) and the Windows tray's root `talos-wsl.sh launch-approve` both compute from supervisor.json as written (agent_dir, claude_path, args, env), the Mac's DesktopConfig.launchFingerprint encoding: SHA-256 over each item as <UTF-8 byte count>:<bytes>, in the order dir, agent_dir, claude, claude_path, args, <count>, ...args, env, <2 x count>, ...key, value rows with the keys sorted by their UTF-8 bytes (code point order). Parts: each piece alone, cut to 8 bytes. Lowercase hex. Computed by an independent Python implementation. Each case says whether supervisor.json is approvable under the strict schema both sides hold to (no defaults: agent_dir and claude_path absolute strings, args a list of strings and required, env an object of strings or absent; claude_path must also be its own real path, which these vectors leave to the machine). A case that is not approvable has no fingerprint to compare: neither side ever approves it. session.id and every session.previous_ids entry must be absent, null or a lowercase UUID (they reach Claude Code's argv as --resume=<id>), but are never hashed: a valid session leaves the fingerprint as it is.",
